---
# Test: syntax-class with non-matching argument
# A syntax class is defined and a macro uses it; passing a non-matching argument
# produces an error with the class's custom message.

[syntax-class identifier-only
  pattern: [let _ : VarRef]
  message: "bare identifier (e.g., x, name)"]

[macro greet [let name@identifier-only]
  [str "Hello, " [unquote name]]]

# Pass a Call instead of a VarRef
[greet [+ 1 2]]

=== error

[E080] macro 'greet': argument 'name' — bare identifier (e.g., x, name), got Call
